            },
            {
                "entry_id": "3f095b5c-7346-301c-8b66-c9fb8b0906eb",
                "word": "woodman",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b7155c2f-5950-453b-be6c-6eeadc7d77be",
                        "entry_id": "3f095b5c-7346-301c-8b66-c9fb8b0906eb",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "woodmen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6ce1f9a5-15c6-30cb-bed4-2dc30af2df55",
                        "entry_id": "3f095b5c-7346-301c-8b66-c9fb8b0906eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who cuts down trees or cuts up, splits, and sells wood."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e4e5481-f906-4545-9172-f838e52d6f90",
                                "sense_id": "6ce1f9a5-15c6-30cb-bed4-2dc30af2df55",
                                "text": "As thro’ the shrilling Vale, or Mountain Ground,\nThe Labours of the Woodman’s Axe resound;\nBlows following Blows are heard re-echoing wide,\nWhile crackling Forests fall on ev’ry side.\nThus echo’d all the Fields with loud Alarms,\nSo fell the Warriors, and so rung their Arms."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfd7c289-c81b-485b-acb6-d5e98070e829",
                                "sense_id": "6ce1f9a5-15c6-30cb-bed4-2dc30af2df55",
                                "text": "Woodman, spare that tree!\nTouch not a single bough!\nIn youth it shelter’d me,\nAnd I’ll protect it now.\n’Twas my forefather’s hand\nThat placed it near his cot;\nThere, woodman, let it stand,\nThy axe shall harm it not!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35acc9ab-6ec9-4725-8faa-0b70979c3a72",
                                "sense_id": "6ce1f9a5-15c6-30cb-bed4-2dc30af2df55",
                                "text": "1862, Percy Bysshe Shelley, “The Woodman and the Nightingale” (written in 1818 and published posthumously) in Richard Garnett (editor), Relics of Shelley, London: Edward Moxon, p. 79,\nThe world is full of woodmen who expel\nLove’s gentle dryads from the haunts of life,\nAnd vex the nightingales in every dell."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3238f11c-064a-333c-9e7b-bf4f116f4f36",
                        "entry_id": "3f095b5c-7346-301c-8b66-c9fb8b0906eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who lives in the wood and manages it; (by extension) someone who spends time in the woods and has a strong familiarity with that environment."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1a79e4f-5cc8-4641-ad35-84b31cd803e7",
                                "sense_id": "3238f11c-064a-333c-9e7b-bf4f116f4f36",
                                "text": "Our walk was far among the ancient trees:\nThere was no road, nor any wood-man’s path,\nBut the thick umbrage, checking the wild growth\nOf weed and sapling […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77a970ea-b89d-4563-8f46-7acc8c766b61",
                                "sense_id": "3238f11c-064a-333c-9e7b-bf4f116f4f36",
                                "text": "“It is strange,” muttered Cardillac, “that so loud a roar in the forest at night should give such little indication of direction. I suppose a true woodman could not only point towards the spot, but might estimate the distance as well. I seem to be a very fool of the forest.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c925f5a9-4d35-442d-bbbd-6134799b5bbc",
                                "sense_id": "3238f11c-064a-333c-9e7b-bf4f116f4f36",
                                "text": "One afternoon, I went with Mrs. Salter-Townshend on a tour of all her rental properties, which ranged from a woodman’s cottage on the old Somerville estate to a tower in the harbor-front castle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "af99e7ea-901e-4fcb-a223-930394fddeea",
                                "sense_id": "3238f11c-064a-333c-9e7b-bf4f116f4f36",
                                "text": "The second examination is for a woodman’s badge. To pass, he is required to light a fire, using no paper and striking no more than three matches."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "422eb684-2059-3b02-9c30-d29c47ea78bd",
                        "entry_id": "3f095b5c-7346-301c-8b66-c9fb8b0906eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who makes things from wood."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1d5e97aa-f479-39b5-99ca-1e33ae9c8eff",
                        "entry_id": "3f095b5c-7346-301c-8b66-c9fb8b0906eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who hunts animals in a wood, hunter, huntsman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b81b5f10-d1e3-401b-8740-8626e2f59fb6",
                                "sense_id": "1d5e97aa-f479-39b5-99ca-1e33ae9c8eff",
                                "text": "You, Polydote, have proved best woodman and\nAre master of the feast: Cadwal and I\nWill play the cook and servant; ’tis our match:\nThe sweat of industry would dry and die,\nBut for the end it works to."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89678049-b4d9-4e64-b980-b83d0461e92e",
                                "sense_id": "1d5e97aa-f479-39b5-99ca-1e33ae9c8eff",
                                "text": "c. 1611, John Fletcher, The Woman’s Prize, Act IV, Scene 3, in Comedies and Tragedies Written by Francis Beaumont and John Fletcher, Gentlemen, London: H. Robinson & H. Moseley, 1647, p. 116,\nHow daintily, and cunningly you drive me\nUp like a Deere to’th toyle, yet I may leape it,\nAnd what’s the woodman then?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0f7f405-c895-4947-bc49-49d93a03b72f",
                                "sense_id": "1d5e97aa-f479-39b5-99ca-1e33ae9c8eff",
                                "text": "1636, Robert Sanderson, Ad Aulam. The Fourth Sermon, Beuvoyr, July, 1636 in XXXVI Sermons, London, 8th edition, 1689, p. 413,\nAnd to get the Mastery over they self in great matters, it will behove thee to exercise this Discipline first in lesser things: as he that would be a skilful Wood-man, will exercise himself thereunto first by shooting sometimes at a dead mark."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "01fa048f-b0a5-3d5b-b19c-679251fe43c1",
                        "entry_id": "3f095b5c-7346-301c-8b66-c9fb8b0906eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who lives in the woods and is considered to be uncivilized or barbaric, a savage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "958aff45-4aa2-43ab-a13f-cf0e95846e03",
                                "sense_id": "01fa048f-b0a5-3d5b-b19c-679251fe43c1",
                                "text": "[…] yonder in that faithfull wildernesse\nHuge monsters haunt, and many dangers dwell;\nDragons, and Minotaures, and feendes of hell,\nAnd many wilde woodmen, which robbe & rend\nAll traveilers […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cd3028d-15bd-4a72-9e3b-af090ffa6171",
                                "sense_id": "01fa048f-b0a5-3d5b-b19c-679251fe43c1",
                                "text": "There between the trees\nThe prying Fauns and Woodmen dark\nAnd prick-ear’d Satyrs her did mark,"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e2545e8e-dc8c-40d6-b914-64952e11f6be",
                        "source_entry_id": "3f095b5c-7346-301c-8b66-c9fb8b0906eb",
                        "source_sense_description": "someone who cuts down trees or cuts and sells wood",
                        "target_lang_word": "bûcheron",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bûcheron",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5d28db4-3637-3b61-b7d3-a8fbfccf91c5",
                                        "entry_id": "2ffc5783-c385-3e0c-9ecb-d8ed4a2e9767",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est propre aux bûcheronnes et aux bûcherons."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d815ec14-191e-4a17-a426-4902e411f914",
                                                "sense_id": "b5d28db4-3637-3b61-b7d3-a8fbfccf91c5",
                                                "text": "Ce lieu, respecté par l’industrie bûcheronne pendant des générations, était devenu aussi sombre que solitaire et l’antique infirmerie des religieux oubliés n’était plus qu’une ruine méchante, un tabernacle de moisissure, de scolopendres et de frissons noirs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06ff8a53-ae13-4495-a246-f0c6ad5fc8af",
                                                "sense_id": "b5d28db4-3637-3b61-b7d3-a8fbfccf91c5",
                                                "text": "[…] et, en fin de compte, de la disparition locale des espèces riveraines subsistant encore par l’agriculture, l’exploitation bûcheronne, le prélèvement du vin de palme, et les feux de brousse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bûcheron",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "761274ae-f92b-333b-88e2-f4c018651b25",
                                        "entry_id": "d92b43f2-2115-3a33-b0f5-6d3c8aaacabd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne dont le métier est de couper du bois dans une forêt."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Métier"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c565c01-a2e4-4c2a-ac99-6090d8906c21",
                                                "sense_id": "761274ae-f92b-333b-88e2-f4c018651b25",
                                                "text": "Comme je paraissais faible et que je boitais un peu, ma mère avait voulu me faire apprendre un métier plus doux que ceux de notre village ; car, au Dagsberg, on ne trouve que des bûcherons, des charbonniers et des schlitteurs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac840195-036b-4e70-a225-24b09c4e7143",
                                                "sense_id": "761274ae-f92b-333b-88e2-f4c018651b25",
                                                "text": "Pendant le décours de la lune, les bûcherons s’occupent à déhoupper les arbres, à faire des bourrées, scier les tiges dans les longueurs qu’on les veut, former leurs chantiers de bois de chauffage, et fendre les culées ; en même temps, les scieurs de long et les charpentiers débitent les pièces ainsi coupées et préparées par les bûcherons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a760cbd2-e076-4f9c-927c-61ca798ae787",
                                                "sense_id": "761274ae-f92b-333b-88e2-f4c018651b25",
                                                "text": "[…] l’ennemi bombardait le bois de Remières. Aplatis promptement contre un talus nous pouvions voir et entendre les obus bûcherons, qui faisaient voler de grosses branches comme des brindilles, après une lueur verdâtre et des explosions déchirantes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03f55c60-cecd-38c7-9062-d5cb2ae17096",
                                        "entry_id": "d92b43f2-2115-3a33-b0f5-6d3c8aaacabd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Meuble représentant le métier du même nom dans les armoiries. La hache est l’attribut distinctif du bûcheron, elle est donc généralement présente et souvent d’un émail particulier. À rapprocher de batteur en grange, faucheur, forgeron, meunier et vigneron."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c3c2e6d-9957-4369-a7d0-5a5379c8131a",
                                                "sense_id": "03f55c60-cecd-38c7-9062-d5cb2ae17096",
                                                "text": "D’argent a deux bûcherons d’azur, sur une terrasse de sinople, découpant un tronc au naturel posé en fasce sur celle-ci, avec chacun une hache d’or, qui est de la famille Arostegui du Pays Basque espagnol → voir illustration « armoiries avec 2 bûcherons »"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
